      "post_id": "2089953694058197408",
      "url": "https://x.com/dereckgoto/status/2089953694058197408",
      "created_at": "2026-08-19T05:52:44Z",
      "text": "This morning, I visited RedHub, RedNote’s Beijing office, for an inside look at one of China’s most influential social media platforms. Its headquarters are in Shanghai.\n\nWhat struck me most was the scale: 400 million+ monthly active users, more than 90% of content is user-generated, and over 70 million new comments every day.\n\nBut the bigger story for Africa is opportunity.\n\nA Ugandan farmer and content creator, Timothy Kiwalabye, joined RedNote in 2025 and saw his everyday African story reach audiences far beyond Uganda.\n\nThat should challenge African creators. China is not only a market for African minerals and commodities - it is also a vast market for African stories, culture, tourism, products and ideas.\n\nAfrica must not only consume the digital world. We must create for it, trade through it and tell our own story to it.\n\nThe platform is built. The audience is there. What's missing is Africa's decision to show up and tell its own story, at scale.",
      "original_text": "This morning, I visited RedHub, RedNote’s Beijing office, for an inside look at one of China’s most influential social media platforms. Its headquarters are in Shanghai.\n\nWhat struck me most was the scale: 400 million+ monthly active users, more than 90% of content is user-generated, and over 70 million new comments every day.\n\nBut the bigger story for Africa is opportunity.\n\nA Ugandan farmer and content creator, Timothy Kiwalabye, joined RedNote in 2025 and saw his everyday African story reach audiences far beyond Uganda.\n\nThat should challenge African creators. China is not only a market for African minerals and commodities - it is also a vast market for African stories, culture, tourism, products and ideas.\n\nAfrica must not only consume the digital world. We must create for it, trade through it and tell our own story to it.\n\nThe platform is built. The audience is there. What's missing is Africa's decision to show up and tell its own story, at scale.",
      "translation_zh": "今天上午，我参观了 RedHub，也就是 RedNote 位于北京的办公室，近距离了解中国最具影响力的社交媒体平台之一。它的总部在上海。\n\n最让我印象深刻的是其规模：月活跃用户超过 4 亿，超过 90% 的内容由用户生成，并且每天有超过 7000 万条新评论。\n\n但对非洲来说，更重要的故事是机遇。\n\n来自乌干达的农民兼内容创作者 Timothy Kiwalabye 于 2025 年加入 RedNote，并看到他关于非洲日常生活的故事触达了远远超出乌干达范围的受众。\n\n这应该促使非洲创作者反思。中国不仅是非洲矿产和大宗商品的市场——它也是非洲故事、文化、旅游、产品和理念的巨大市场。\n\n非洲不能只是消费数字世界。我们必须为它创作，通过它进行贸易，并向它讲述我们自己的故事。\n\n平台已经搭建好。受众就在那里。缺少的是非洲决定大规模地现身，并讲述自己的故事。",
      "translation_status": "translated",
